{{also|naive}}

==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|naïve|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|nativus||native, natural|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/naɪiv/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Lacking [[experience]], [[wisdom]], or [[judgement]].
#: ''Surely you're not '''naïve''' enough to believe adverts!''
# {{context|of art}} Produced in a simple, [[childlike]] style, deliberately rejecting [[sophisticated]] techniques.
#: ''I've always liked the '''naïve''' way in which he ignores all the background detail.''

====Synonyms====
* see [[WikiSaurus:naive]]

====Antonyms====
* see [[WikiSaurus:naive]]

====Derived terms====
* [[naïf]]
* [[naïvely]]
* [[naïveness]]
* [[naïveté]]

